            "body": "I'm not sure if the actions failure stems from this or not.\r\nI think not.\r\n\r\nRunning the tests locally with:\r\n`cmake --build build --target functionaltest__vimscript`\r\n\r\nI see:\r\n\r\n```\r\n-------- Running tests from test/functional/vimscript/fnamemodify_spec.lua\r\nRUN      T123 fnamemodify() root path: 57.74 ms OK\r\nRUN      T124 fnamemodify() ~user in a fast event #40707: 55.15 ms OK\r\nRUN      T125 fnamemodify() :8 (DOS 8.3 short format): 51.92 ms OK\r\nRUN      T126 fnamemodify() examples from \":help filename-modifiers\": 55.00 ms OK\r\nRUN      T127 fnamemodify() advanced examples from \":help filename-modifiers\": 53.28 ms OK\r\nRUN      T128 fnamemodify() :h: 54.86 ms OK\r\nRUN      T129 fnamemodify() :t: 51.71 ms OK\r\nRUN      T130 fnamemodify() :r: 54.50 ms OK\r\nRUN      T131 fnamemodify() :e: 52.60 ms OK\r\nRUN      T132 fnamemodify() regex replacements: 53.35 ms OK\r\nRUN      T133 fnamemodify() shell escape: 51.64 ms OK\r\nRUN      T134 fnamemodify() can combine :e and :r: 53.22 ms OK\r\n-------- 12 tests from test/functional/vimscript/fnamemodify_spec.lua (645.98 ms total)\r\n```\r\n\r\nMaybe the task should be rerun?\r\n\r\nEdit:\r\naint no way that one bounds check is breaking the entire build 😵‍💫 and now hanging the CI too\r\nwhat curse did I bring with me, it Worked on my Machine™",
